  "id": "recipient-pin.behavior.tofu",
  "kind": "recipient-pin.behavior",
  "milestone": "M6",
  "title": "TOFU claims a first-use pin inside reserve, admits the matching recipient thereafter, refuses a changed one as pin-mismatch, and fails closed when TOFU is not provisioned",
  "spec": ["SPEC §6", "SPEC §6.1", "SPEC §6.2", "SPEC §3.4", "ADR-028"],
  "description": "TOFU is enabled for merchant-b. B1 reserves with no pin yet and recipientEnforcement tofu: the claim happens in the reserve atom and recipientPinEstablished is true (exactly one worker would emit recipient.pinned). B2 pays the same recipient and is admitted with recipientPinEstablished:false — the pin already exists, so no re-claim (the replay-safety guard). B3 pays a changed recipient and is refused TX402_RECIPIENT_UNPINNED reason pin-mismatch (source=tofu), with the RP-8 details. The pin readback shows the single claimed recipient. Finally merchant-c has recipientEnforcement tofu but TOFU was never provisioned, so its reserve fails closed with TX402_CONFIG_INVALID reason recipient-tofu-not-provisioned (SPEC §6.1) rather than silently admitting.",
